 Oh, Georgia. We've talked about Georgia, of course.

5
00:01:59,380 --> 00:02:07,690
 Do you remember? It was in 1733 that General Oglethorpe, an idealist, landed there with about a hundred men who'd been in debtor's prison.

6
00:02:07,970 --> 00:02:11,950
 And they were Lutherans and Swiss and Scots and Jews and even women.

7
00:02:12,230 --> 00:02:15,280
 And together with them, they founded Savannah, Georgia.

8
00:02:16,960 --> 00:02:20,290
 One of you has to work with his own hands.

9
00:02:20,290 --> 00:02:22,310
 There will be no slaves, no alcohol.

10
00:02:24,530 --> 00:02:38,590
 As it happened a few years later,

11
00:02:38,590 --> 00:02:41,590
 in this period there are one and a half million Europeans on American soil,

12
00:02:41,590 --> 00:02:44,590
 but this population would double every 20 years or so.

13
00:02:44,590 --> 00:02:48,880
 As for cities, well, only a few ports were worthy of the name:

14
00:02:48,880 --> 00:02:54,060
 Boston, and Philadelphia, and New York, Charleston.

15
00:02:54,060 --> 00:02:57,550
 And all the rest were no more than, well, communities.

16
00:02:57,550 --> 00:03:08,030
 So 300,000 blacks in the South, who it's understood are supposed to be freed after six or seven years, but things didn't always work out that way.

17
